cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  BayesianRAG: Bayesian Orchestration of Tool-Augmented Agents
message: >-
  If you use this software or reference its results, please cite it
  using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Angshul
    family-names: Majumdar
    email: angshul@iiitd.ac.in
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering,
      Indraprastha Institute of Information Technology Delhi
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX'  # add your ORCID before release
repository-code: 'https://github.com/AngshulMajumdar/BayesianRAG'
abstract: >-
  Tool-augmented language model agents select actions greedily and recover
  from failure by retrying; both follow from maintaining a single execution
  trajectory, so evidence arriving later has no surviving branch to promote.
  BayesianRAG formulates agent execution as sequential inference over action
  trajectories, exposing deterministic greedy selection, probabilistic forward
  sampling, and Bayesian sequential Monte Carlo as inference strategies over
  one generative model. Particles carry per-trajectory Beta-Bernoulli beliefs
  over tool reliability with retroactive credit assignment, answer selection
  is ordered by validation status rather than recency, and posterior mass is
  marginalised over answers to yield a calibrated criterion for requesting
  clarification. On stochastically unreliable tools the method converts a
  source correct one call in ten into a system correct nine times in ten.
keywords:
  - bayesian-inference
  - sequential-monte-carlo
  - particle-filter
  - llm-agents
  - tool-use
  - retrieval-augmented-generation
  - rag
  - agent-orchestration
